POSIX (Portable Operating System Interface)

A set of standard APIs, command-line tools, and shell behavior that operating systems should follow so that software written for one POSIX-compliant system can run on another without modification.

You can have at least one of the followings:
Dual Boot
Least recommended. (https://ubuntu.com/, https://linuxmint.com/)
VM
Virtual Machine, such as Virtual Box (or VMWare) (https://www.virtualbox.org/)
Windows Subsystem for Linux (https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/)
Cygwin (https://cygwin.com/)
Mingw-w64 (https://www.mingw-w64.org/)
GCP (https://cloud.google.com/)

